WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.000
What Lies Behind That Emotion

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.970
You're so weak!

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.460
Come on, come at me again — with all you've got!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.700
Well?!

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:14.710
<i>That's</i> all you've got? No way!

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:33.340
If you're this weak, then there's no need for you, Gourai.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:40.520
Bye bye!

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.440
Winner: Hresvelgr

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.220
Jeez, I won again.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.360
Beating puny Data Models like this one is boring.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.710
I want to hurry up and fight the <i>real</i> Gourai.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.670
Huh...

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.170
This'll be fun.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.680
You!

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.800
You're Gourai's master, right?

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.560
How strange for a human to come pay a visit.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.310
Um, I'm here today because I wanted to ask-

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.120
Stop!

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.230
There's somewhere I want to go.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.630
Come with me.

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.860
Huh. There's a place like <i>this</i> here?

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:56.580
They say we're not allowed to come here <i>alone.</i>

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.600
But if you're with me, I'm not alone, right?

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.490
Say, Hres...

00:04:08.250 --> 00:04:11.140
Why did you say such terrible things to Gourai?

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:12.630
"Terrible things"?

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:17.180
Yeah. Like, she'll be recalled,
or that you'll beat everyone.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.560
Is that really "terrible"?

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.100
And you took me hostage!

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.690
Oh. Because Gourai wasn't giving it her all.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:27.470
Jeez, did you come here just
to talk about boring stuff like this?

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.320
It's not boring at all!

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:31.700
When you say things like that, everyone...

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:33.970
Including Gourai...

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:38.450
I'm home.

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.590
Huh?

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.130
What is all this?!

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.370
Ao!

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:48.700
I swear... When Gourai saw that you'd left
while she was recharging, she just went nuts.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.920
You see? I told you she'd only gone
to the convenience store.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:54.600
Ao, it's dangerous for you to go out alone!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.550
It's okay, Gourai. It's right down the street.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.650
No!

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.360
If Hresvelgr comes back...!

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.770
Ao, you mustn't leave my sight!

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:08.610
Huh? What about school?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:09.520
I'll go with you.

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.610
And the bathroom?

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.610
I'll go with you.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:12.440
Forget it!

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.650
Fine, then leave the door open.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.880
Gourai! There's no way I can live my life that way!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.370
But if something were to happen to you again...

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.050
I... I have to protect you!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.500
You may have been followed.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.300
I'll go take a look outside!

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.190
Everyone, please look after Ao!

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.960
What a pain.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:37.910
Ao-chan.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.860
C'mon, can't you do something about Gourai?

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:44.640
There's nothing that can be done.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:48.450
After all, she has grown appropriately.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.200
She has?!

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:55.180
The one who taught Gourai-chan
about emotions... was you, Ao-chan.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.930
Why did you think such emotions
would only go one way?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.670
Joy...

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.170
Pain...

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.540
Happiness...

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.130
Sadness...

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.500
Reassurance...

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.650
Anxiety...

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:15.220
The happiness and contentment she now holds dear...

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.030
...bring with them the fear and loneliness
of not wanting to lose them.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.400
Oh. So, Gourai is...

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.390
We wish to ask something.

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:28.450
As Gourai-chan's master...

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.360
What do you want to do?

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.300
I...

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.240
I want to know.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:42.360
You'd be able to battle Gourai without
going through all this, so why do it?

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.850
Everyone who's arrived so far has been able to battle.

00:06:45.850 --> 00:06:49.330
"Everyone"? You mean,
those other weaklings at your place?

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:51.750
Jeez! Stop saying those things!

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.010
Those guys are a separate team.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.210
A separate team?

00:06:55.210 --> 00:06:57.630
Yup. But I'm different.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:00.140
No matter how many of those
other guys there are, it's no use.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.350
So, there's only one of you?

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:03.890
Well, of course!

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.830
You don't need a whole bunch of <i>me,</i> do you?

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:09.750
But isn't that lonely?

00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:13.200
What does "lonely" mean?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:19.990
Fine, let me ask you:
why are there so many of those other guys?

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:24.460
Well... they hold battles,
talk amongst themselves, have fun-

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.090
Why? There's no point.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:35.400
There is! Gourai has learned so many things
by being together with the others.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:37.970
So what?

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.220
That's just meaningless.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:45.470
We are what we are; trying to mimic
human ways won't come to anything.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.730
It's not like you're just mimicking us...

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:51.610
They say we have unlimited potential.

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.190
We can become anything, do anything.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.320
Those others don't get it at all!

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:01.640
A Frame Arms Girl should be proud and self-reliant.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:04.410
Some people say that, huh?

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:08.500
Yup! That's why I'm on my own, and I like it that way.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.080
Still, my first battle with Gourai was fun.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:16.320
I didn't know how different she was
from the Data Models.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.840
I wonder if the company will hurry up
and tell me to head out there again.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:27.100
Oh, but if I crush Gourai and those others,
I guess I'll have to keep fighting the Data Models.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.230
Still, that wouldn't be so bad.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.730
You like fighting, don't you?

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:34.650
Well, of course. I love battles!

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.400
Fighting powerful enemies is super fun!

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:39.160
Otherwise, it's just boring.

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:43.290
That's why I'll be going to your place again.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:47.880
But before I do, tell Gourai
she has to get much, much stronger!

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:49.520
Okay.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.730
See you again, Hres.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:04.730
What's this?

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.510
I wonder if they'll make me even stronger!

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:11.110
I look forward to facing those guys soon!

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:21.950
A Public Bath! A Battle?!

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.960
Ao? What's the matter?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.280
Bukiko...

00:09:27.280 --> 00:09:29.780
Gourai has turned into such a worrywart.

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:32.000
She follows me to the bath, the toilet...

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:33.090
...and school.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:40.900
When I go to sleep, there's a string
around my pinky that's tied to her.

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.360
I have no freedom!

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.600
That's tough, Ao.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:49.500
Still, that's a pretty serious illness she's got...

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.790
Ah, that's it!

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.530
What's that?

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.400
Something good!

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.450
sentou
A public bath...

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:03.900
Yeah! Bukiko gave me
a single-day ticket to Ume-no-yu.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.660
Let's all go and have a relaxing time!

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.660
sentou
A battle? Sounds great!

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.170
No, that's not it.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.600
Public baths are...

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.090
Architect, help me out.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.520
Learning Mode: "Public Bath."

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.470
Data acquisition complete.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:28.730
A communal bathing facility with changing rooms
and large, separate bathtubs for men and women.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:31.720
It is a place for patrons to relax and interact.

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:32.980
You hear that?

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:37.420
Let's all go and have a relaxing soak
in some hot water...

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:39.900
Ao, you big dummy!

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:42.650
Have you forgotten that we can't go in the water?

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:45.110
Yup. Water is off limits!

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:46.500
O-Oh...

00:10:46.980 --> 00:10:48.400
So, a public bath is out?

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:51.990
There is nothing to prevent us from going,
but we cannot enter these "bathtubs."

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:53.380
Indeed.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:58.540
We'll get to have a good, long look at Ao-chan
without a stitch of clothing on.

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:02.220
And we just might do unspeakable things to her.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.570
Ao. We should use this opportunity.

00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.630
There's no way to make it work.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.310
No, there is.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:14.620
I have confirmed that within the Battle Stage directory,
there is a hot springs area.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.650
This can be inferred to be a
Frame Arms Girl bathing facility.

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.310
Huh?! I've never once seen that!

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:23.020
It can only be accessed through random encounter.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:24.580
So it's no good.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:28.430
Wrong, just leave it to the genius, Base-sama!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.630
I'm not sure about this, but...

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:34.640
I <i>do</i> want to take a bath with you all.

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:37.170
Please help us, Base!

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.730
Let's all go the public bath!

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.760
Yeah!

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.350
Big baths are the best!

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:58.230
Well, let's get things ready.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:00.890
Like this?

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:03.960
Over here, you won't get any water
splashed on you, so you'll be safe.

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:06.960
It's a good thing Jinrai Session Base is fixed, huh?

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:07.650
Indeed.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:10.370
It has been refined and is now even better than before!

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.790
Well, let's get started!

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.530
Gourai!

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:14.520
Stylet!

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:15.860
Baselard!

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:16.650
Jinrai!

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.020
Architect!

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:19.620
Materia!

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:22.420
Frame Arms Girl: Public bath!

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:37.600
Not bad.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.460
It's wonderful!

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:41.520
Architect, good job!

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:44.530
Still, that's only how it <i>looks,</i> right?

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:49.880
H-Huh? What is this feeling?

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.580
It's warm somehow...

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.010
and soft!

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:57.610
I changed it up a bit and made it so it can recharge us.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:00.100
And at a higher voltage.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:02.090
To the very limit.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:03.960
This feels great.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.340
Sure enough, Japanese people prefer <i>this,</i> huh?

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.020
This is the life...

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:53.060
I will... I <i>will</i> win!

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:57.100
I swear, Gourai. There you go again.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:03.610
But, but if I do lose, I won't be able to do things like
come with you to a public bath, or talk and have fun.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.520
It will all... everything will...!

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:06.380
Stop!

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:10.340
If you lose, that's one thing, but this is another.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:13.080
But we could all be recalled!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.740
Not to worry. If they don't send us back to Ao,

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:20.250
I'll threaten to pull out every screw
and nail in the company!

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.490
We could also turn the higher-ups into our servants...

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:26.510
...making it so that their bodies are dependent on us.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.320
Why not use an evasive attack?

00:14:29.320 --> 00:14:30.380
Or copy their data.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.510
Please think about this a little more seriously!

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:40.270
Gourai. Everyone's coming up with ideas.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:44.270
This is Hres we're talking about,
so let's all think of something together.

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:49.020
We won't come up with a surefire way
of beating her right off the bat, but...

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.410
we can't just keep our feelings to ourselves.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.990
Your happiness grows when you talk to someone else,

00:14:56.990 --> 00:15:01.540
and if you're sad, talking about it helps you feel better.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.670
So let's <i>talk</i> to one another.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.000
But can I properly say what I-?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:06.920
You'll be fine!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:08.340
Just blurt it out!

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:13.650
Um, I... I...

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.590
I love you, Ao.

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:19.380
All of you.

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:23.110
Even Bukiko and the building manager, and Ni-taro.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.010
Where did that come from?

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:27.640
Sty, she's saying she loves <i>you</i> too!

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:28.150
H-Hey!

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.030
I love you as well, Stylet.

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:35.650
I've learned so many emotions since being with you all.

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:38.790
And I hold several new memories inside me.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:44.020
I love our life here. I don't want to lose it!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:47.520
That's why I want to try my hardest — together!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:04.870
Hey, Gourai-chan!

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:07.600
Gourai-chan, I swear.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:09.030
She's blushing.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.860
Will Architect be all right?

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.280
Well, she's worn out.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:17.490
That's just meaningless.

00:16:18.230 --> 00:16:20.260
It's not meaningless.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:25.520
After all, Hresvelgr, <i>you</i> were the one
who said you wanted to fight Gourai.

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:31.170
That means that even you
think it would be better to have friends.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:33.430
Ao.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.920
You want a coffee milk? Or a fruit-flavored <i>milk?</i>

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:40.680
Me-no-yew's recommendation is apparently...
Durian-flavored milk!

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.940
I'll take something normal!

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.060
They'll soon show up at your door,

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:53.460
for my special someone, parts of hearts!

00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:03.740
Counting the days I can't see you,

00:17:04.930 --> 00:17:11.190
I want to hear your voice so badly I feel like crying!

00:17:11.190 --> 00:17:14.680
I'm new to this world,

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.150
so I lack the language to describe it.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:20.420
To knockoffs, say...

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:23.870
"No!" Take care to avoid them.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:27.390
I want to be be dedicated!

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:36.090
I want to build it all from nothing!

00:17:36.090 --> 00:17:39.320
We laugh and we fight,

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.930
creating our unique specs!

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:48.850
By mixing love and hate,

00:17:48.850 --> 00:17:56.920
I want to create more of these funny, carefree days, the parts of Girl!

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:17.150
Coming!

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:18.290
Huh?

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:20.630
Whoa!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.110
Oh, my.

00:18:26.110 --> 00:18:27.500
A guest?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.280
Whose Charger-kun is that?

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:30.380
Beats me.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.600
It's mine.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.980
Hresvelger!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:36.980
I presume it wasn't rude.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.590
Now then: let's begin.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:44.240
Hold on! Where do you get off wandering in
and battling like it's perfectly normal?!

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:49.140
She has... a different air about her now...

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:52.100
Are you really Hresvelgr?

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:54.320
I am Hresvelgr=Ater.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.390
"Ater"?

00:18:55.390 --> 00:19:00.150
It would seem that this time she's upgraded
not just her weapons, but her entire body.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.950
I have a bad feeling about this...

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:03.780
Yes. Very bad.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.570
Gourai, come on.

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:09.440
I want to fight you so badly that I can't stand it.

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:10.900
Gourai...

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.430
I'll be back.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.640
Gourai!

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.090
Hresvelgr=Ater.

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:21.210
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.430
Go!

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.000
If Gourai loses this battle...

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:29.880
She and the rest of us will be
recalled to Factory Advance.

00:19:29.880 --> 00:19:31.360
But she's gonna win, right?

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:32.980
Of course she will!

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:34.260
Really for real?

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:37.350
I don't wanna be separated from Ao!

00:19:37.350 --> 00:19:39.990
Neither do I! It would be too sad...

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.730
So, Styko-chan would get sad.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.020
How cute.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.570
Do you need me to pat you on the head?

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:48.870
N-No, I don't!

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:52.200
I sure would be sad if you all left.

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:55.130
That's why, I definitely want Gourai to win.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:20:00.560
But... maybe Gourai shouldn't fight.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:01.380
Huh?

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:25.870
Hresvelgr! You-!

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:34.330
This upgrade was your idea?

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:37.270
Yes. But it's still lacking.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.590
I'm not strong enough. No, it won't do.

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:44.090
I want to beat you a million times over.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:46.550
Is that what this battle means to you?

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:48.500
There is no meaning.

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:49.310
I have no need of it...

00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:52.760
not of the battle, not of you,

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:53.810
and not even of myself!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:20:58.860
Gourai!

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.390
She's so powerful, isn't she?

00:21:00.390 --> 00:21:01.810
But she's different.

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:02.780
Ao?

00:21:03.180 --> 00:21:05.530
I mean, Hres said so herself...

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.440
I love battles!

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:10.490
Fighting powerful enemies is super fun!

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:14.750
But now, she doesn't seem like
she enjoys anything at all.

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:19.840
She's not fighting because she wants to;
they're making her fight to collect data!

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:22.510
But how did that happen?

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:36.190
Hresvelgr! Look at me.

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:39.190
What are talking about? Shut up.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:43.440
Please look at me when you're... fighting me.

00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:48.620
I told you...

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:50.860
to shut up!

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:06.010
What is it? What's going on?

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:09.130
Perhaps her power isn't regulated.

00:22:09.130 --> 00:22:10.860
Analyzing conditions.

00:22:12.090 --> 00:22:15.060
The upgrade to her enhancement program
has been given run priority.

00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:17.560
The result: Overflow.

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:20.900
The nanomachines inside her body are running wild!

00:22:35.430 --> 00:22:36.970
Hresvelgr!

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:46.080
The lines we cry out for our battles
were actually taken from Ao's poems.

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:47.000
Huh?!

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:47.030
That Which I Give to You
Last Battle
Huh?!

00:22:47.030 --> 00:22:47.540
Last Battle
That Which I Give to You

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:49.630
On the next Frame Arms Girl,

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:51.170
let's have another session together!

00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:54.620
Well, that's fine. It's one of the things I love about you!

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:55.000
Last Battle
That Which I Give to You
